# CP522 B-r3 source repair handoff

The exact four allowed Windows source files are committed at `fec4a4d7bc8aa4ce6ee1e0f9a7da024bd528ca3f` (tree `730be49f57988da8be32af27225848690d202e63`) on `codex/qualification-failure-b-r3-20261015`. The worktree was clean at finalization. `FINAL-manifest.json` pins all nine combined source hashes, the four-file delta from `1d3cc504da79df5bf0f69755011738d5adb827b0`, and the whole nine-file patch from `f48fca0e`.

F01: The directory guard now opens every ancestor and the final directory with `FILE_LIST_DIRECTORY | FILE_READ_ATTRIBUTES | READ_CONTROL`, without `FILE_SHARE_DELETE`; the original independent rename/swap repro failed on the base and passes after the repair. The metadata-only Windows handle did not block a namespace rename. Native file IDs and bytes are rechecked while the handles remain held.

F02: `HoldQualificationNativeFacts` retains the original `bridge.json`, `stdout.raw`, `stderr.raw`, rejection JSON, and selected MODEL Host fact handles. The private consumer rereads and binds raw hashes, exact rejection bytes, canonical frames and payload, dispatch, broker, observation, and MODEL DB binding. `validatedQualificationFailureTx` returns an opaque `qualificationFailureClosure`; callers must call `Check()` before accepting it and `Close()` only after the transaction has ended. The online creation path holds its native originals through writes and actual `COMMIT`, and releases in a deferred close on every path. Replay paths roll back before closing the returned closure. The previous private return contract changed intentionally; any future caller must observe this lifetime rule.

The original independent B-r2 domain overlay was adapted only at its private-consumer helper to receive the closure, call `Check`, and `Close`. The original reviewer source remains unchanged. The adaptation is `independent_b2_domain_release_windows_test.go`; `post-fix-domain-overlay.json` selects it. It keeps the 87-table logical census, exact five versions plus one upload, replay zero logical delta, seven MODEL database cuts, and four original raw cuts. Both independent overlays pass after the repair. Own domain and adapter qualification matrices pass; original pinned Mu three groups pass with zero skips. `gofmt -l` for the four files and `git diff --check` returned empty output and exit 0. The pre-fix F01/F02 failures, sparse-fixture setup failures, initial disk-full checkout failure, and two original command-capture gaps are preserved in `diagnostic-ledger.jsonl` without rewriting raw outputs or counters.

`command-index.json` gives argv, cwd, UTC times, exit, and SHA-256/byte counts for 73 captured commands. `claim-test-matrix.json` points to raw pre-fix and after-test outputs. `CP522-bootstrap-{invocation,raw,exit}` records the successful first scope/AGENTS read; the two earlier bootstrap/ledger capture gaps have only original tool results and are explicitly classified. The local worktree used a sparse checkout after an ordinary checkout exhausted D: disk; no original production, database, provider, Ollama, or persistent review state was changed.

Cleanup of this branch's reproducible `0.44 GiB` temporary Go cache under `.local/qualification-failure-b-r3-20261015-tmp` was attempted only after resolving and checking the exact target. Automatic command review rejected the recursive `Remove-Item`; the cache remains intact. No deletion workaround was used.

Authority boundary: this is a source repair plus local and independent-overlay evidence. It is **not** independent B-r3 acceptance or actual/formal acceptance. `formal_increment=0`, `actual_authority=false`, `independent_review=PENDING`, and `self_acceptance=false`. Exhaustive foreign-SID and hostile-race interleavings, exact 15-second drain timing, and full cleanup Cartesian cases were not newly proven here.

Relevant Windows API references: [CreateFileW](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/fileapi/nf-fileapi-createfilew) and [File access rights constants](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/fileio/file-access-rights-constants).

